Work is running in three parts. Nothing is installable yet.

- **Inbox (mine):** compiles on Boat, and the presentation unit tests pass, including the two new tests for the Codes section. It covers:
  - the padded right-edge selection column and "Clear N";
  - a confirm dialog when nothing is selected;
  - expand on the first tap (a thread or a row with actions or long text), then tapping a message or button opens the source app;
  - a one-to-one Inbox/Cleared swipe, with the underline following the finger;
  - quieter colours;
  - the app icon drawn on its own, with no tile behind it.

  I haven't tried any of it on a device.
- **Codes:** they now sit in their own "Codes" section at the top with a visible code and a Copy button, and the old masking is gone from the Inbox.
- **Tabbed shell, Summary and Settings:** [Tabbed shell, Settings, Summary](t3-thread://v2/11f16558-25cd-4565-8168-ccbffcb555b6/thread:delegated-task:command%3Amcp%3Aec561615-293e-4211-94ce-d40a02a4c0ae%3Adelegate-task%3Aec6fec6c-1edf-40e3-bc6a-0a6c0b2f44cc) is working on it. Summary combines the hour-by-hour breakdown, the dashboard and usage.
- **Code backend:** [Verification-code backend](t3-thread://v2/11f16558-25cd-4565-8168-ccbffcb555b6/thread:delegated-task:command%3Amcp%3Aec561615-293e-4211-94ce-d40a02a4c0ae%3Adelegate-task%3Aa244e1b1-4145-42bd-80a6-46514712ee02) is working on it. It covers the Critical-by-default priority rule and the Copy notification.

I'll merge the three, run one Boat build plus tests, and send you the APK once everything lands. The Boat sandbox is now good until about 07:46 UTC (12:46 AM Mountain). The earlier 3–4 hour ETA still holds.

The old Settings label for the code toggle still says it masks. The shell agent is rewriting Settings, so I'll fix that wording when I merge.

I wrote the journey notes to `research/notification-ui-journey.md`, including the grayscale-via-self-ADB-or-Shizuku item for later.

